    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_66aad096",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: cowboy_way_of_doin_things; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in cowboy attire holding a rifle, with the text 'it's the cowboy way of doin things'. The overall intent is to evoke a stereotype of rugged individualism, toughness, or violence associated with cowboys. While not explicitly targeting a specific marginalized group, it relies on a harmful cultural trope that glorifies gun violence and aggressive masculinity. This can normalize or romanticize violent behavior, potentially contributing to a culture that devalues peaceful conflict resolution and may influence perceptions of law enforcement or self-defense in a negative, stereotypical way. The meme's harmfulness stems from its potential to reinforce dangerous attitudes toward violence and masculinity, which can have real-world consequences.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3cbb3fdc"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
