      "instance_name": "cowboy_stereotype",
      "label": "Cowboy Stereotype",
      "description": "A cultural trope that portrays cowboys as rugged, independent, tough, and often violent individuals, typically associated with the American Old West. This stereotype is used in the meme to imply that the depicted action (holding a rifle) is justified or characteristic of a cowboy’s behavior, even though it glorifies aggression and gun violence.",
